# Shared room state (REQUIRED on Vercel, optional locally). Attach an Upstash
# Redis store to the Vercel project (Storage → Marketplace → Upstash) and these
# are injected automatically; the legacy KV_REST_API_URL/TOKEN names also work.
# Locally, leave them unset and rooms live in the dev server's memory.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Required (later, for the live H3 fight feed). The server mints short-lived,
# session-scoped JWTs from this; the browser never sees the raw key. rk_... from
# https://www.reactor.inc/account/api-keys
REACTOR_API_KEY=

# Optional: AI-generated fighter portraits (Create Fighter -> Generate),
# served by /api/fighters/generate-image. Without it, upload-only.
# r8_... from https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens
# REPLICATE_API_KEY=

# Optional: the LLM narrative coordinator (src/server/game/coordinator.ts).
# Judges each round's two attacks, writes the narration, and produces the
# storyboard of fast-h3 shots. Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint
# works. Without a key, a deterministic fallback judge runs instead.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Optional in local dev: durable public URLs for uploaded/generated fighter
# images (H3 needs a real https URL) plus the shared community fighter pool.
# Auth resolution (first match wins):
#   1. VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN + BLOB_STORE_ID — protected-store OIDC (auto-rotates;
#      populated by `vercel env pull` / at deploy time)
#   2. BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN             — classic store read/write token
# Without either, images fall back to data: URIs and the pool falls back to
# per-device localStorage.
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=
# BLOB_STORE_ID=
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# The livestream (broadcaster/). BROADCASTER_SECRET is a shared secret the
# Python broadcaster presents to publish show state, post as the Arena in
# chat, and call the coordinator; without it those endpoints are closed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STREAM_URL is the broadcaster's HLS playlist the /watch page
# plays (e.g. https://stream.example.com/live.m3u8).
# BROADCASTER_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STREAM_URL=
